3. Authentication & Session Persistence Logic
Gatekeeper Gateway: The landing view restricts site access behind a security barrier requiring a universal group passcode (123).
Token Dropper: Upon validation, the application must drop a persistent client session cookie or localStorage token (wedding_session_token: true) configured with a 60-day post-event expiration timeline.
Bypass Engine: On layout load, a root lifecycle check must verify if the active session token exists. If valid, the gatekeeper access screen is entirely skipped, and the main scrolling feed mounts immediately.
Typo Tolerance: If a guest corrects a spelling mistake in their first or last name inside their Profile Sheet, the system must execute an atomic database UPDATE on their row without invalidating or clearing their active device session token.
